= Data repository — Simple =

A data repository is an infrastructure or service for depositing, preserving, describing, discovering, accessing, and stewarding datasets or other research data.

Repositories may be institutional, disciplinary, general-purpose, or project-specific. They commonly provide metadata, persistent identifiers, access controls, versioning, preservation procedures, and citation support.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* data repository ≠ database
* repository deposit ≠ preservation guarantee

